{"title":"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2a899df14e2d9806cb21a05abfacd741e15448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^6 - 3x^5 - 6x^3 - x + 8 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"213\" height=\"16\" /> has\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc619abe170c0cac343000e79fbd0af54c4b9ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ no real roots} \\\\ \\textbf{(B)} \\text{ exactly two distinct negative roots} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)} \\text{ exactly one negative root} \\\\ \\textbf{(D)} \\text{ no negative roots, but at least one positive root} \\\\ \\textbf{(E)} \\text{ none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Really_Smart.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Really_Smart)\">Solution 1 (Really Smart)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Really Smart)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a9917a7fb271cdc3d7a3fbb9669ebeef98711d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^6 - 3x^5 - 6x^3 - x + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a68e8aa6ec6f48231ad80a4851f84bacf641b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/7527ae05697ff38b4ae941844cd02735c9242304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, there are no negative roots. \n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecd8c473b69b898b1fb710c0edd3a5087bb4bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/5485c20f4e91678542a95a03c560760ca9b132c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(0) = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />. There must be at least one positive root between 0 and 1, therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\nSidenote&#160;: If anyone is wondering what this method is called,\n</p>\n<pre>It is called the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c052bb09c6d061c531d18dd8bd6ef9c0f188d07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf {squeeze theorem}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />\n</pre>\n<p>~Aarav22\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1975 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a h